<h2>How to Compress Large PDF Files for Email Attachments (Under 25MB / 10MB)</h2>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> Learn how to reduce PDF file size below 25MB for Gmail or 10MB for Outlook. Compress large scanned PDFs and presentations online without losing text readability.</p>
<p><strong>URL:</strong> https://www.mypdf4u.com/blog/how-to-compress-pdf-for-email</p>
<h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
<h4>How do I make a PDF file smaller than 25MB to send via Gmail?</h4>
<p>Upload your file to MyPDF4U's Compress PDF tool, select 'Balanced' compression, and click Compress. It reduces image bloat and outputs a file that easily fits within Gmail's 25MB ceiling.</p>
<h4>How much file size reduction can I expect?</h4>
<p>Scanned documents, photos, and presentation slides typically shrink by 50% to 80%. Pure text PDFs with no images are already compact and will see modest reductions.</p>
<h4>Will compressing a PDF make the text blurry?</h4>
<p>No. With Light and Balanced compression, text and line art maintain clear readability on all desktop and mobile screens.</p>
<h4>Is the PDF compressor free with no file limit?</h4>
<p>Yes. The tool is 100% free with no account creation, no watermark, and no artificial daily conversion limits.</p>
<h4>Can I compress password-protected PDF files?</h4>
<p>You must unlock the PDF first. Use our free [Unlock PDF tool](/unlock-pdf) if you know the password, then compress the unlocked copy.</p>
