<h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
<h4>How do I combine PDF files for free without Adobe Acrobat?</h4>
<p>Use MyPDF4U's Merge PDF tool. It is 100% free, requires no Adobe subscription, and works directly in your web browser with zero uploads.</p>
<h4>How do I merge PDF files on Windows 10 / 11?</h4>
<p>Open www.mypdf4u.com/merge-pdf in Edge or Chrome, drag in your PDF files from File Explorer, arrange their order, and click Merge PDFs.</p>
<h4>How do I combine PDF files on Mac for free?</h4>
<p>Open the first PDF in Preview, show the Thumbnails sidebar (View → Thumbnails), drag your second PDF into the sidebar, and save via File → Export as PDF.</p>
<h4>How can I merge PDF documents on iPhone?</h4>
<p>In the iOS Files app, tap '...' → Select, choose your PDF files, tap '...' at the bottom right, and select 'Create PDF'. Or use MyPDF4U in Safari.</p>
<h4>Is there a limit on how many PDFs I can merge?</h4>
<p>No arbitrary file count limits exist on MyPDF4U. You can merge 2, 10, or 50+ documents depending on your device memory.</p>
<h4>Does merging PDFs lower the text or image quality?</h4>
<p>No. Pages and vectors are merged byte-for-byte without re-compressing or degrading resolution.</p>
<h4>Are my merged documents safe and private?</h4>
<p>Yes. Processing takes place entirely inside your browser using client-side JavaScript. Your files are never uploaded to any server.</p>
