<h2>How to Make a Scanned PDF Searchable with OCR</h2>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> Turn a scan or photographed document into a PDF you can search and copy from. How OCR works, how to feed it good input, and what to expect.</p>
<p><strong>URL:</strong> https://www.mypdf4u.com/blog/how-to-ocr-scanned-pdf</p>
<h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
<h4>What is OCR in a PDF?</h4>
<p>Optical character recognition reads the words in a page image and adds them to the PDF as a text layer, so the document becomes searchable and copyable.</p>
<h4>Which languages are supported?</h4>
<p>English, Spanish, French, German, Portuguese, Italian and Dutch. The matching language data downloads once, the first time you run OCR.</p>
<h4>Why does OCR take longer than other tools?</h4>
<p>Every page has to be rendered and analysed rather than simply copied, and all of that work happens on your own device.</p>
<h4>Will the document look different afterwards?</h4>
<p>No. The page image is unchanged; the recognised text sits behind it so it can be searched and selected.</p>
<h4>Can OCR read handwriting?</h4>
<p>Not reliably. It is designed for printed text; handwriting and decorative fonts produce many more errors.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>How to Split a PDF and Extract the Pages You Need</h2>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> Pull single pages or ranges like 1-3, 7 out of a PDF, or break a document into separate files. Page-range syntax explained with practical examples.</p>
<p><strong>URL:</strong> https://www.mypdf4u.com/blog/how-to-split-pdf-pages</p>
<h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
<h4>How do I extract a single page from a PDF?</h4>
<p>Type its page number in the page ranges field — for example 4 — and click Split PDF. You get a one-page document.</p>
<h4>Why did I receive a ZIP file?</h4>
<p>When a split produces more than one PDF, the files are bundled into one ZIP so it stays a single download.</p>
<h4>Does splitting reduce quality?</h4>
<p>No. Pages are copied into the new documents as they are, with no re-compression.</p>
<h4>Can I split a password-protected PDF?</h4>
<p>Not directly. Remove the password with the Unlock PDF tool first, then split the unlocked copy.</p>
<h4>How do I split every page into its own file?</h4>
<p>Leave the page ranges field empty. Each page is saved as a separate PDF inside the ZIP.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>How to Rotate PDF Pages and Save the Change</h2>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> Fix sideways or upside-down scans permanently — rotate every page or only the ones that are wrong, and download a file that opens the right way up.</p>
<p><strong>URL:</strong> https://www.mypdf4u.com/blog/how-to-rotate-pdf-pages</p>
<h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
<h4>How do I rotate a PDF and save it permanently?</h4>
<p>Use the Rotate PDF tool, choose an angle and download the result — the rotation is written into the document rather than into your reader's view.</p>
<h4>Can I rotate only one page?</h4>
<p>Yes. Type its number in the pages field, for example 3, or a mix such as 1, 4-6.</p>
<h4>Does rotating reduce quality?</h4>
<p>No. The page content is untouched; only its orientation flag changes.</p>
<h4>Will other apps see the rotation?</h4>
<p>Yes, because it is stored in the PDF itself, so readers and printers both honour it.</p>
<h4>How do I rotate different pages by different amounts?</h4>
<p>Run the tool once per angle, listing the relevant pages each time.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>How to Reorder and Delete Pages in a PDF</h2>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> Rebuild a PDF with the pages you want, in the order you want. One page list handles reordering, deleting and even duplicating pages.</p>
<p><strong>URL:</strong> https://www.mypdf4u.com/blog/how-to-organize-pdf-pages</p>
<h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
<h4>How do I delete a page from a PDF?</h4>
<p>List every page except the one you want gone. To remove page 2 of a ten-page file, type 1, 3-10 and rebuild.</p>
<h4>Can I duplicate a page?</h4>
<p>Yes — list the same page number twice, for example 1, 1, 2.</p>
<h4>What happens if I leave the page order empty?</h4>
<p>You get a copy of the document with its original page order preserved.</p>
<h4>Is the original file changed?</h4>
<p>No. A new PDF is built in your browser and downloaded; your source file is untouched.</p>
<h4>Can I rotate pages at the same time?</h4>
<p>Yes. The rotate option applies to all the pages you keep, so a whole batch of sideways scans can be fixed in one pass.</p>
